// Phase 6.5b-2. The integration service definition.
//
// It exposes the restricted integration projection and NOTHING else. The buyer
// projections ZJP_C_PurchaseOrder and ZJP_C_PurchaseOrderItem stay on
// ZJP_UI_PURCHASEORDER, where they belong; a single service carrying both
// surfaces would mean one binding, one set of authorizations and one blast
// radius for two consumers with opposite needs.
//
// Named for its purpose rather than for its entity: the service exists so the
// supplier's answer can reach SAP. It is also deliberately not named
// ZJP_API_PURCHASEORDER, which would collide with the projection view entity
// above once ABAP upper-cases both.
@EndUserText.label: 'Purchase Order Supplier Response API'
define service ZJP_API_SUPPLIERRESPONSE {
  expose ZJP_API_PurchaseOrder as PurchaseOrders;
}
